id: SECRETS-057
ilities: [confidentiality]
maturity: 1
source: cpm
title: Vercel Access Token
category: secrets
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .tsx .js .jsx .py .java .go .rb .rs .cpp .h .cs .php .env .yml .yaml .json .toml .xml .properties .cfg .ini .conf .sh .tf .hcl
  exclude_paths: test/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/ __pycache__/ .venv/ target/
  content_contains: vercel
patterns:
  # 1. Modern prefixed tokens (Vercel 2026-02 format, visually identifiable):
  #    vcp personal / vci integration / vca app / vcr refresh / vck API key,
  #    followed by the token body. The prefix is a strong, low-false-positive
  #    anchor. https://vercel.com/changelog/new-token-formats-and-secret-scanning
  - regex: \bvc[piark]_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
    message: Vercel access token/API key detected (prefixed format). This grants access to deploy, configure, and manage Vercel projects.
  # 2. Legacy 24-char tokens had NO prefix, so a bare [A-Za-z0-9]{24} matched
  #    anything (lockfile integrity hashes, ids, …). Require a credential
  #    CONTEXT instead: an assignment to a vercel/token-looking key. This keeps
  #    the catch for real `VERCEL_TOKEN=...` while dropping the mass false
  #    positives measured on package-lock.json etc.
  - regex: (?i)vercel[a-z0-9_]*(?:token|key|secret)[a-z0-9_]*\s*[:=]\s*["']?[A-Za-z0-9]{24}\b
    message: Vercel access token detected (legacy format in a credential assignment). This grants access to deploy, configure, and manage Vercel projects.
fix: Revoke the token at Vercel > Settings > Tokens. Create a scoped token and store it in CI/CD secrets or environment variables.
